  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Runtime",
      "items": [
        "A client-only single-page app: no server code in this repo",
        "A HashRouter serves /, /projects and /terminal; unknown addresses go home",
        "Home, Projects and Terminal use the same symmetric page padding (120px top and bottom) and the body has none, so each glass panel is centred on the window's middle line, level with the centred site menu",
        "All three pages put their panel on one shared glass-panel class from the plain stylesheet src/styles/glass.css (no CSS Modules composes across files): same width, blur, border and monospace font. The home panel adds roomier inner padding; it holds the name, the role subline and the newest project (projects[0]); the name button toggles the cat",
        "The four hidden Poke Balls are spread over the whole home glass panel: one in the top padding, one in the left padding, one in the bottom padding and one beside the subline text. Below 1300px and under 700px each gets a narrower-window position so none sits on the name, link or screenshot. They come last in document and tab order, with the counter just above the panel's top edge",
        "Home and the social bar read the name, role and links from src/data/profile.ts, the same file the terminal's about and contact use",
        "The only persisted state is the colour index in localStorage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Terminal",
      "items": [
        "A fake shell in plain React on /terminal, with no new dependency: type a command, read the answer",
        "The logic is pure and unit-tested: parser, commands, shell, virtual filesystem and Tab completion import nothing from React; Terminal.tsx is only the view",
        "The scrollback (500 lines), the folder and the history (500 commands) live in a SessionProvider above the routes, so they survive a visit to another page. They are memory-only: a reload starts a fresh session",
        "The virtual filesystem is generated from the data modules, so a new project, job or school becomes a file with no further change",
        "open <page or project> navigates through the menu list and the project ids; theme <colour> sets the real site theme; matrix only previews the other colours and never stores them, so a reload mid-run keeps the visitor's own colour",
        "play returns a game effect; Terminal.tsx then switches the pane from the shell to the Game. play skip prints the career as plain text instead"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Game: Career Quest",
      "items": [
        "A Game Boy style adventure opened by the play command, drawn on a canvas inside the terminal panel; the build of the town, rooms, people and battles comes from the same data as the virtual filesystem",
        "The engine is pure: step(state, input, world) returns the next state plus text events and sound cues, and imports nothing from React. useGameLoop runs it at a fixed 60 ticks a second and, with reduced motion, advances one whole move per key press",
        "The progress and the mute switch live in the terminal session, so leaving the game or visiting another page keeps them; neither is ever written to storage. A reload starts at the title",
        "The canvas is hidden from assistive technology on purpose: a polite live region tells the story, and Skip to text prints the career",
        "Pixel art is generated: scripts/sprites turns pixel definitions into three indexed PNG sheets and atlas.ts, and npm run sprites -- --check fails when the committed files differ",
        "Sound is synthesised on Web Audio with no audio files: scores are text, a sequencer hands out notes just ahead of the clock, the director picks the tune for the moment, and M mutes. A missing or failing AudioContext never reaches the game"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Theme",
      "items": [
        "The matrix colour and the site theme are one index, owned by ThemeProvider",
        "cycle and select store the index; preview shows a theme for now without storing it, and a real choice ends it",
        "main.tsx applies the stored theme before React renders, then turns the fade on",
        "CSS files read --accent tokens on html, the shared glass stylesheet included; clicking the rain changes them all"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Delivery",
      "items": [
        "Every push and pull request runs check, build and e2e",
        "Deploy needs all three and runs only on main",
        "The custom domain and HTTPS live in the Pages settings, not in a file"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Tests",
      "items": [
        "Vitest unit tests sit beside the code in src/, including theme contrast and token use, every terminal module, and the game's engine, renderer, loop and audio",
        "Playwright tests the exact dist the build job produced, on desktop and mobile, terminal page included",
        "The game pilot plays the page by key presses and steps a copy of the engine alongside, so a test can ask to walk to a door instead of listing keys"
      ]
    }
  ]
